      title: '+ How do you navigate workers\' compensation requirements and determine appropriate surgical referral criteria?',
      content: '**Workers\' Compensation Management**:\n\n**Documentation Requirements**:\n1. **First report of injury**: Ensure this has been filed with the employer and workers\' comp carrier. Include date, time, mechanism, and witnessed status.\n2. **Medical records**: Thorough documentation of mechanism (acute traumatic event at work), objective exam findings, imaging results, and functional limitations. This establishes causation and medical necessity.\n3. **Work status reports**: At each visit, document specific work restrictions using standard terminology (sedentary, light, medium, heavy). Provide modified duty restrictions when possible.\n\n**Work Status for This Patient**:\n- **Currently**: Sedentary duty only. No use of right upper extremity for lifting, carrying, pushing, or pulling. If modified duty is available (administrative tasks), he can work. If not, temporary total disability.\n- **If conservative**: Light duty by 6-8 weeks. Medium duty by 12-16 weeks. Full duty pending FCE at 20-24 weeks.\n- **If surgical**: No work for 6-8 weeks. Sedentary/light duty by 8-12 weeks. Medium duty by 16-20 weeks. Full duty pending FCE at 6-9 months.\n\n**Surgical Referral Criteria**:\n1. Full-thickness tear confirmed on MRI\n2. Functional limitation preventing return to pre-injury work duties\n3. Good tissue quality (Goutallier Grade 0-2) suggesting repairable tear\n4. Reasonable surgical candidate (medically fit)\n5. Workers\' comp authorization may require a trial of conservative management (typically 6 weeks) before approving surgery — varies by jurisdiction.\n\n**Authorization Process**:\n- Submit pre-authorization request to workers\' comp carrier with supporting documentation (MRI report, exam findings, failed conservative care if applicable)\n- Independent medical examination (IME) may be requested by the carrier\n- Utilization review may question surgical necessity — be prepared to support with evidence-based guidelines (ACOEM Practice Guidelines)\n- Peer-to-peer review may be needed if initially denied\n\n**Return-to-Work Planning**:\n- **Functional Capacity Evaluation (FCE)**: Order before full-duty return. Objective measurement of the patient\'s ability to meet the physical demands of his specific job.\n- **Work hardening/conditioning program**: If FCE reveals gap between current capacity and job demands, 2-4 week structured program to bridge the gap.\n- **Permanent impairment rating**: If residual deficits remain at maximum medical improvement (MMI), calculate impairment rating per AMA Guides (6th edition). This determines any permanent partial disability settlement.',
